  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Look at your phone to unlock it. It is comparing your face with a stored representation. Many phones project a pattern of infrared dots that your eyes cannot see. An infrared camera reads how that pattern bends across your face. Those distortions become a depth map describing shape rather than skin color. The system converts distinctive shape information into a mathematical face template. It compares the new template with the template created during enrollment. If they are close enough and liveness checks pass, the phone unlocks. The phone is not simply matching a photograph. It is checking a secure representation of your face.",
